{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"habitual-fleshy-prawn","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Config-driven type mapping + type-granular skip (collapse round-trip via rebar-type label)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nTicket-type mapping is hardcoded (`value_maps.LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`) and whole-type sync\nexclusion is a fixed set (`config.EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`). A Jira project that lacks a rebar\ntype (e.g. no `Story`) has no configured recourse today: it can't remap the type to an\nanalog (Epic→Initiative) and can't cleanly skip the missing type. Type must become\nconfig-driven on the S1 core with three outcomes: **remap**, **skip** (type-granular\nwhole-ticket exclusion), and **fail-closed** on an unmapped-non-skipped type. Because\nrebar may have more types than Jira, a **non-injective collapse** must be allowed and made\nround-trip-safe via a new `rebar-type:` annotation label, symmetric with `rebar-status:`.\n\n## Approach\n\nWire the S1 `type_map` axis. Outbound: resolve the effective type map over the built-in\ndefault (`LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`); a mapped type is remapped; a type whose config value is\nthe sentinel `skip` extends the excluded-from-sync behavior (`EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`) at\nper-project granularity; an **unmapped, non-skipped** type is a **fail-closed load error**\n(surfaced by S1 `validate`) — never a silent drift. When distinct rebar types collapse to\none Jira type, stamp a `rebar-type:<local>` label (new, mirroring the existing\n`rebar-status:` label machinery in `inbound_fields.py`) so inbound recovers the original\nrebar type. Inbound: prefer the `rebar-type:` label, else invert the effective map.\nDocument the hierarchy consequence: collapsing to a same/lower Jira hierarchy level\nforfeits the parent role, so children fall to the S7 breadcrumb path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py` — type resolution + per-project skip.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` — built-in\n  default becomes injected fallback.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py` — `rebar-type:` label recovery.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_type_mapping.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Config-effect contrast (unit):** with `type_map.epic=\"Initiative\"`, an outbound epic\n  targets `Initiative`; default targets the built-in value — same path, different config.\n- **Skip (per-project):** a type mapped to `skip` excludes that type's tickets from sync\n  for that project only; another project still syncs it — asserted on the sync decision.\n- **Fail-closed (failure path):** an unmapped non-skipped type raises the named validation\n  error at load; the nearest valid config does not raise.\n- **Round-trip (collapse):** collapsed types stamp `rebar-type:` labels; inbound recovers\n  each distinct rebar type.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Effective type map = built-in ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>`; a non-default overlay\n  changes the outbound type through the real path — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_type_config_effect`.\n- [ ] A `skip`-mapped type excludes that type from sync per-project only — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_type_skip_per_project`.\n- [ ] An unmapped non-skipped type fails closed at load with a named error — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_unmapped_type_fails_closed`.\n- [ ] Collapsed types round-trip losslessly via `rebar-type:` labels — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_type_collapse_roundtrip`.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — type resolution, skip decision, and label round-trip are\npure functions; oracles are the produced type field, the sync decision, the raised error,\nand the recovered type.","id":"a8ea-be28-2394-4f0c","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Config-driven type mapping + type-granular skip (collapse round-trip via rebar-type label)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290314049994001,"uuid":"b7438d8f-3126-4b22-ae37-079c138b413c"}